    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0944" n="930" sameAs="frus:frus1946v06/pg930"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/8–2846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-28T16:00:00+01:00">August 28, 1946—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 28—2:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4300. Delsec 867. From the Secretary for
                        Clayton.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d657-f1"/> In the light of recent
                    developments I want you to do everything that we properly can to stop further
                    shipments of supplies of any sort by UNRRA for
                    Yugoslavia. I think you will realize the implications of an organization to
                    which the United States contributes 73% continuing to supply a government guilty
                    of such outrageous and unfriendly conduct as Yugoslavia.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d657-f2"/></p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d657-f1" n="38" xml:id="d657-f1-content">
                <p>William L. Clayton, Under Secretary of State for Economic Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d657-f2" n="39" xml:id="d657-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 4329, Delsec 872, August 29, from
                    Paris, reported that Secretary Byrnes had requested that the War Department be
                    asked to halt the transfer of any ammunition whatsoever to the Yugoslavs
                    (740.00119 Council/8–2946).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
